  ${
    $d s t f x y $.
    $( A magma homomorphism is a function on the base sets which preserves the
       binary operation.  (Contributed by AV, 24-Feb-2020.) $)
    df-mgmhm $a |- MgmHom = ( s e. Mgm , t e. Mgm |->
          { f e. ( ( Base ` t ) ^m ( Base ` s ) ) |
            A. x e. ( Base ` s ) A. y e. ( Base ` s )
                  ( f ` ( x ( +g ` s ) y ) )
                  = ( ( f ` x ) ( +g ` t ) ( f ` y ) ) } ) $.

    $( A submagma is a subset of a magma which is closed under the operation.
       Such subsets are themselves magmas.  (Contributed by AV,
       24-Feb-2020.) $)
    df-submgm $a |- SubMgm = ( s e. Mgm |-> { t e. ~P ( Base ` s ) |
                             A. x e. t A. y e. t ( x ( +g ` s ) y ) e. t } ) $.

