  ${
    $d a b c g l p v $.
    $( TODO - this could be generalized to posets! $)
    $( Define class of all right ordered monoids.  An ordered monoid is a
       monoid with a total ordering compatible with its operation.  It is
       possible to use this definition also for left ordered monoids, by
       applying it to ` ( oppG `` M ) ` .  (Contributed by Thierry Arnoux,
       13-Mar-2018.) $)
    df-omnd $a |- oMnd = { g e. Mnd | [. ( Base ` g ) / v ].
      [. ( +g ` g ) / p ]. [. ( le ` g ) / l ]. ( g e. Toset /\
      A. a e. v A. b e. v A. c e. v ( a l b -> ( a p c ) l ( b p c ) ) ) } $.

    $( Define class of all ordered groups.  An ordered group is a group with a
       total ordering compatible with its operation.  (Contributed by Thierry
       Arnoux, 13-Mar-2018.) $)
    df-ogrp $a |- oGrp = ( Grp i^i oMnd ) $.
  $}

