       many of our other examples of closure systems, this one is _not_ usually
       an algebraic closure system ~ df-acs : consider the Hilbert space of
       sequences ` NN --> RR ` with convergent sum; the subspace of all
       sequences with finite support is the classic example of a non-closed
       subspace, but for every finite set of sequences of finite support, there
       is a finite-dimensional (and hence closed) subspace containing all of
